WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.835
-They love you.
We love you. Welcome back.

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:06.172
Congrats. July 4th.
I'm excited about the premiere.

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.173
-Yeah.

00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:08.808
-It's good to hang
with you guys.

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:09.842
-Good to be back.

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:11.110
-I'm happy you are back.

00:00:11.110 --> 00:00:12.712
And Sadie,
I've never met you.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.547
-Yeah, it's my first time here.
-Nice to meet you.

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:15.882
-Yeah, nice to meet you.

00:00:15.882 --> 00:00:18.418
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.219 --> 00:00:22.221
-Let's talk about
the new season,

00:00:22.221 --> 00:00:23.289
and things that
we can tell people

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.191
that isn't
spoiling anything.

00:00:25.191 --> 00:00:27.627
I know a lot of it was shot
in a mall.

00:00:27.627 --> 00:00:28.928
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.930
Was it a real mall?
-It was a real mall, actually.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.131
-It was?
-It was, yeah.

00:00:32.131 --> 00:00:33.900
It was, like, this mall --
-A working mall?

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:35.468
-It was, actually.
-Technically.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.503
-It is, still, actually.
-Technically.

00:00:37.503 --> 00:00:39.039
-Technically.

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:40.806
-It was a little haunted.
-A little bit.

00:00:40.806 --> 00:00:42.341
-Every time we'd be in there,
it'd be fine.

00:00:42.341 --> 00:00:44.743
And then, we'd all just kind of
look at each other, and be like,

00:00:44.743 --> 00:00:46.479
"Something wrong
with this mall."

00:00:46.479 --> 00:00:47.580
[ Laughter ]

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:49.215
And it kind of helped.
-Yeah.

00:00:49.215 --> 00:00:50.316
-Yeah.

00:00:50.316 --> 00:00:52.118
-The thing is,
it's still operational.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.253
Even though they, like, bought,
like, a piece of the mall,

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:56.222
and, like,
they redid it totally...

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.890
-It's incredible.
-Like, a whole --

00:00:57.890 --> 00:00:59.158
It looks gorgeous.
It's amazing.

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:00.693
I think people
still go there, now.

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:01.827
-Yeah.
-And just, like, look around.

00:01:01.827 --> 00:01:03.029
But, like --
-Well, how much fun is that,

00:01:03.029 --> 00:01:04.597
to be in an empty mall?
-It's so cool.

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:05.965
But it's not even empty.
-So fun.

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:08.501
-Like, a bunch of people are
shopping as we're filming.

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:11.136
in the mall, people are shopping
as we're filming.

00:01:11.136 --> 00:01:14.206
[ Indistinct talking ]

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:16.543
-And, like,
I see people just like...

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:17.743
[ Laughter ]

00:01:17.743 --> 00:01:19.645
...looking in.
Like...

00:01:19.645 --> 00:01:21.847
Serious, like,
spoilers happening.

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:23.383
Like, major plot points.

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.084
-Don't tweet this!
Don't tweet this!

00:01:25.084 --> 00:01:26.252
-But, like,
serious plot points.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.420
They're just looking.
They're like, "Huh."

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.054
-'Cause it's, like,
an active --

00:01:29.054 --> 00:01:31.190
sometimes, our trailers
are in active parking lots.

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:33.393
And so, someone will just
drive in and be like,

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.428
"Is this the Keith Urban
concert?"

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:36.529
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:37.997
And they'll
just be like --

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.132
And they'll just
be like,

00:01:39.132 --> 00:01:40.666
"No. This is a working set."

00:01:40.666 --> 00:01:42.435
And they're like,
"Alright."

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:43.803
And they roll up --
They don't even care.

00:01:43.803 --> 00:01:45.938
-[ Speaks indistinctly ]
-Yeah, I guess.

00:01:45.938 --> 00:01:48.407
-But I heard that you --

00:01:48.407 --> 00:01:51.344
you would actually go
up and down the escalators...

00:01:51.344 --> 00:01:52.912
-Yeah.
-...as slides.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.246
-Yeah.
-That was my idea.

00:01:54.246 --> 00:01:55.849
-That was your idea?
-Bad idea.

00:01:55.849 --> 00:01:57.216
-Oh, it was a bad idea?
-Great, good i--

00:01:57.216 --> 00:01:59.852
bad, good idea, whatever.
-It was a great idea.

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:02.522
-Well, like, the ADs and stuff
that were in charge of us,

00:02:02.522 --> 00:02:03.756
they would say
it was a bad idea.

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.357
-The space in between...
-The escalator.

00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:06.526
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:07.994
He started sliding down it.
Then, we all did.

00:02:07.994 --> 00:02:09.762
And then, the production team
hated us for it.

00:02:09.762 --> 00:02:11.998
-Yeah.
-But, no, went went against --

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.265
-I moved the
barrier cones

00:02:13.265 --> 00:02:14.367
-Yeah.
-They put cones,

00:02:14.367 --> 00:02:15.801
but then,
we moved the cones.

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:19.472
[ Indistinct talking ]

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:21.640
-It was a giant slide. 'Cause
usually, they have, like...

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:22.942
-Little things stopping you.
-...the little things
stopping you.

00:02:22.942 --> 00:02:24.677
They didn't have that.
-No, they didn't.

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:25.945
But then, at the end,
they did.

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:27.680
-And it was, like, greasy.
-Yeah.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.149
It was.
-But what was cool is that,

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:30.616
we kept doing it.
They told us to stop.

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:32.585
So, we stopped for, like,
a couple weeks.

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:35.554
And then, we started
doing it again, 'cause...

00:02:35.554 --> 00:02:36.990
-I didn't stop.
-You didn't stop.

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.057
-I kept going.
-He never stopped, no.

00:02:39.057 --> 00:02:41.727
[ Indistinct talking ]

00:02:41.727 --> 00:02:43.028
-I forget who it was
who suggested it,

00:02:43.028 --> 00:02:45.197
but, like, everyone's like,
"No. Stop."

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:46.533
And then, all of a sudden,
they're like,

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.968
"Hey. Slide down that
for the shot."

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:50.937
-It was Maya.
It was Maya.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:52.071
-Well, I mean,
Maya suggested it,

00:02:52.071 --> 00:02:53.606
but, like, everyone was,
like, super down with it

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:55.074
except for the ADs.
-Oh, of course.

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:56.709
-The ADs were like,
"Do not slide down that.
It's dangerous."

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:58.377
-I distinctly
remember Caleb --

00:02:58.377 --> 00:03:00.546
someone going, "Caleb,
please do not slide down it."

00:03:00.546 --> 00:03:01.714
And him just going...

00:03:03.883 --> 00:03:05.351
-Oh, wow.

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.553
-While giving this
straight face, he's like...

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:08.955
-They hated you for that.

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.256
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:11.390
-And then,
I just slide down.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.792
-It seems like you guys,
like, bonded so much

00:03:13.792 --> 00:03:15.661
on all these seasons.

00:03:15.661 --> 00:03:16.996
I mean,
it's kind of fun,

00:03:16.996 --> 00:03:18.397
because it's, like,
really, I could feel --

00:03:18.397 --> 00:03:20.833
-Specifically over disobeying.
-Yeah. Exactly. Of course.

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:22.234
Yeah. Did you -

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.269
You came in last season,
but do you feel like

00:03:24.269 --> 00:03:25.371
you're part of
the family now?

00:03:25.371 --> 00:03:27.240
-Yeah.
I feel like I am.

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.175
I think I fit in okay,
I guess.

00:03:29.175 --> 00:03:31.777
-You definitely are. I mean,
I know you guys get together,

00:03:31.777 --> 00:03:35.915
and just joking backstage,
we were all just --

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.383
there's always, like,
10 bits going on.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:38.884
Someone's doing a bit,
and then, someone's laughing

00:03:38.884 --> 00:03:41.053
at some other bit. And then,
someone's singing a song.

00:03:41.053 --> 00:03:42.388
What is this song
that you invented?

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:43.455
Caleb, you.
-Oh.

00:03:43.455 --> 00:03:45.524
Another invention of mine.

00:03:45.524 --> 00:03:46.792
[ Indistinct talking ]

00:03:46.792 --> 00:03:48.294
-Do you think you
invented sliding?

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:50.262
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.262 --> 00:03:52.264
-Yes. He invented sliding.

00:03:52.264 --> 00:03:54.466
-Technically, on our set,
you invented sliding.

00:03:54.466 --> 00:03:55.868
-On our set.
-Okay.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.203
-On our set.
-Yeah.

00:03:57.203 --> 00:03:59.305
-What's the song?

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.539
-"Chicken Noodle Soup."

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:03.109
It's a song that I made
to annoy Gaten and Sadie.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:04.610
-It works.
-It definitely works.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:05.811
[ Indistinct talking ]

00:04:05.811 --> 00:04:07.380
-And then, you started barking,
and annoying us.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:09.248
-They didn't like it,
but then, they joined in.

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:11.083
-Then, we joined in.
-Yeah.

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:12.418
-Do you want to hear it?

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:14.386
-I would like to.
What does it sound like?

00:04:14.386 --> 00:04:15.655
What is the name
of the song?

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.156
-"Chicken Noodle Soup."
-"Chicken Noodle Soup."

00:04:17.156 --> 00:04:18.925
-And it's annoying?
-Oh, God.

00:04:18.925 --> 00:04:20.592
-Yeah. It was just a song
to annoy them.

00:04:20.592 --> 00:04:22.328
You guys ready?
-Ready.

00:04:22.328 --> 00:04:24.230
-Ready?
One, two...

00:04:24.230 --> 00:04:29.368
-Three.
-♪ Chicken noodle soup ♪

00:04:29.368 --> 00:04:33.105
♪ I feel good
when you're around ♪

00:04:33.105 --> 00:04:38.377
-Oh, God.
-♪ Chicken noodle soup ♪

00:04:38.377 --> 00:04:42.248
-That's on key, Roots.
-♪ ...when I'm down ♪

00:04:42.248 --> 00:04:46.485
♪ Chicken noodle soup ♪

00:04:46.485 --> 00:04:50.756
♪ I feel good
when you're around ♪

00:04:50.756 --> 00:04:54.927
♪ Chicken noodle soup ♪

00:04:54.927 --> 00:04:57.029
♪ [Indistinct] ♪

00:04:57.029 --> 00:05:01.400
♪ When I'm down ♪

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.237
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:09.041
-That's just a beautiful...
-I know.

00:05:09.041 --> 00:05:10.876
-That's just a beautiful,
beautiful song.

00:05:10.876 --> 00:05:12.378
[ Indistinct talking ]

00:05:12.378 --> 00:05:14.447
-I feel like I'm at
a Keith Urban concert.

00:05:14.447 --> 00:05:16.549
-No, no,
that's one parking lot down.

00:05:18.117 --> 00:05:21.420
How would you explain
the new season?

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.088
Again, I'm just so
excited about that.

00:05:23.088 --> 00:05:25.090
Netflix, by the way,
did not sneak me any episodes,

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.326
which, normally, I get...
-Which is so rude.

00:05:27.326 --> 00:05:29.728
-Right?
I mean, Netflix,

00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:31.364
I can keep a secret
better than anyone.

00:05:31.364 --> 00:05:32.464
-Uh...

00:05:32.464 --> 00:05:34.000
[ Indistinct talking ]

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.402
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:37.970
-By the way, Millie,
how's your toe?

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.338
-Oh, my Go--
[ Laughs ]

00:05:39.338 --> 00:05:40.573
-What?

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:43.342
-Last time I was here,
Jimmy stepped on my toe,

00:05:43.342 --> 00:05:44.577
trying to sabotage me.

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:46.178
-No, I did not. I did not.
-Yeah, you did.

00:05:46.178 --> 00:05:47.212
Don't deny it.

00:05:47.212 --> 00:05:49.114
-[Indistinct]...choreographed
a dance.

00:05:49.114 --> 00:05:52.184
-On the plane after,
I was, like, icing.

00:05:52.184 --> 00:05:53.719
No.
-No, I stepped back,

00:05:53.719 --> 00:05:55.454
and I'm like, "Ooh."
And then, I was like --

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:56.522
-And then, I, like,
looked at you,

00:05:56.522 --> 00:05:58.524
and I was like...

00:05:58.524 --> 00:06:00.092
I still engaged
with the Roots.

00:06:00.092 --> 00:06:01.794
I was like,
"Guys, bring it back up for me."

00:06:01.794 --> 00:06:02.995
-Yeah, yeah.
-And all of a sudden,

00:06:02.995 --> 00:06:04.730
boom, my toe, like...

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:05.998
-But it's
recovering now?

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:08.100
-Yeah, it's recovering.
It's slowly recovering.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.434
We'll see.

00:06:09.434 --> 00:06:11.437
-Without giving away spoilers,
can we sum up, maybe,

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.405
the new season
in one word?

00:06:13.405 --> 00:06:14.540
I thought you
could do that,

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:15.841
and that wouldn't
give anything away.

00:06:15.841 --> 00:06:17.844
And we could start with Finn,
and go all the way down.

00:06:17.844 --> 00:06:20.146
Can you sum up the new season
in one word?

00:06:20.146 --> 00:06:21.547
-Classic.

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:23.582
Does that make sense?
-Yeah.

00:06:23.582 --> 00:06:25.317
-Caleb?

00:06:25.317 --> 00:06:29.121
-Um, you know, gory, prob--
yeah, gory.

00:06:29.121 --> 00:06:30.223
-Sadie?

00:06:30.223 --> 00:06:31.957
-Fun.

00:06:31.957 --> 00:06:35.394
-That's wildly different
from Caleb's answer.

00:06:35.394 --> 00:06:36.495
Gory and fun.

00:06:36.495 --> 00:06:37.797
-Finn is doing more
than one word.

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:39.097
-Uh...

00:06:39.097 --> 00:06:40.299
spreading.

00:06:40.299 --> 00:06:41.366
-What?
-What?

00:06:41.366 --> 00:06:43.202
-Spreading?
-Spreading.

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:44.803
-Spreading?
-Spreading.

00:06:44.803 --> 00:06:46.572
-It makes sense -- It makes
sense once you see it.

00:06:46.572 --> 00:06:47.706
-You guys know
what it means.

00:06:47.706 --> 00:06:48.841
-No.
-Yes, you do.

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.009
-It makes sense
once you see it.

00:06:50.009 --> 00:06:51.010
-I have no clue
what you're talking about.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:53.546
-Okay, alright,
spreading.

00:06:53.546 --> 00:06:54.646
-Sad.

00:06:54.646 --> 00:06:56.349
-Oh.

00:06:56.349 --> 00:06:57.949
-Wow!

00:06:57.949 --> 00:07:01.353
Wow!
What a reaction "sad" got!

00:07:01.353 --> 00:07:03.089
It's so sad.
-I said "gory."

00:07:03.089 --> 00:07:04.423
That's pretty sad, guys.
-Yeah.

00:07:04.423 --> 00:07:06.926
"Classic" -- "Classic"
and "gory" are off the table.

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:09.061
But "sad" --
now, you've got me.

00:07:09.061 --> 00:07:11.864
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:14.166
-Bigger.

00:07:14.166 --> 00:07:16.034
-Oh.

00:07:16.034 --> 00:07:17.937
[ Indistinct talking ]

